**If that reading is right, the triangulation compares a truncation-corrected estimate against an uncorrected one.** They are not the same estimand, and the gap between 0.52 and 0.66 is partly a methods difference rather than an accuracy difference. That is a genuine inhomogeneity in the triangulation — different from the confound I withdrew, and not addressed by CL-AUD-021's caveat list.

